Dear Ms. Crawford,

The records for LP-25-04 are ready. Attached are the release letter MFB-PRO-2=
0260112-001 and three electronic records: the issue specification, the nine s=
ubmitted quotations, and the staff evaluation and recommendation. Those recor=
ds comprise 46 numbered pages.

The three paper records are the purchasing intake register, the Library servi=
ce terms jacket, and the selection routing jacket. You may collect those 30 p=
ages at the Public Records Office counter from 2:00 p.m. today. Together the =
six records comprise 76 numbered pages. The letter is separate from that coun=
t and lists the page ranges for each record.

Sincerely,

Dorothy Hensley
Public Records Office
Mapleton Falls Borough

